course: dictionary
lesson: 14927
title: Refute: proving an idea wrong
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To refute something is to prove that it is wrong. It is a verb, so it changes: refute, refutes, refuted, refuting.
explain: «The test refuted the claim that plants can grow in the dark.» The test showed the claim was wrong, so refute means prove wrong. Check it by swapping in your meaning: «The test proved the claim was wrong» still makes sense.
explain: In science, debates and news lessons, you refute a claim with evidence, such as results or facts. «Maya refuted Sam's argument by showing the photo of the real sunflower.» Her photo was the proof that Sam's idea was wrong.
fact: Refute is a verb: refute, refutes, refuted, refuting.
fact: «Refute» means to prove that an idea, claim or argument is wrong.
fact: Common phrases are refute a claim and refute the argument.
fact: In formal writing, «refute» can also mean to say firmly that something is not true, even without proof.
fact: Refuting is about showing the idea is wrong, not just saying you dislike it.
exercise: «The experiment refuted the idea that heavy things always fall faster.» What does refuted mean here? | Proved right | *Proved wrong | Copied exactly
exercise: In class, Leo wants to refute the argument. What is he trying to do? | Write the argument out neatly on the board | *Prove the argument is wrong | Agree with the argument and praise it
exercise: Nadia said the news story was false, but she had no proof. «Nadia refuted the story.» What did she do? | Agreed with it and added more details | Copied it into her notebook | Forgot it at once | *Said firmly that it was not true, even without proof
test: «The scientist refuted the theory with a clear result.» What does refuted mean here? | Proved the theory was right | Wrote the theory down neatly | *Proved the theory was wrong
test: Maya refutes Sam's idea today. Yesterday she ___ a different idea. Which word fits the gap? | *refuted | refuting | refute | refutes
exam: Which sentence uses refute correctly? | The team refuted the song quietly | The team refuted the sunny weather at dinner | *The team refuted the claim by testing it with a real experiment | The team refuted lunch and ate it quickly
